meta { title = "Built-in functions", description = "Alphabetical index of every public built-in call and numeric conversion.", order = 0, group = "Library reference" }

Built-ins are functions available without an import. Use the alphabetical index to look up a name, or choose a reference by topic. Record and enum constructors, operators and control-flow keywords are described in the language reference. range(...) is available as allocation-free for-loop syntax; import its factory from std/iter to store and reuse a Range value.

